    "summary": "I built a seed-starting tray of four hex cells packed close together at level 0: (0,0), (1,0), (0,1) and (1,-1). Each cell has a half-depth bin with drain holes in the floor, a shallow depth that suits seedlings. I ran the house rules: 14 solid end caps close the open outer faces and 5 joint bolts hold the cells together. That makes 22 parts, about 1777 g of filament and about 2594 minutes of printing. To show what it's for, each bin is filled with soil and has a seedling planted in it. These are display props only and aren't in the parts list. The final check found no rule errors, no warnings about the props, and the collision check came back clear.",
